# Plan: Rebuilding the ML-KEM-768 Specifications From Mathematical First Principles

## Purpose and stance

This document is a **clean-slate plan**. It **discards every existing
specification** for the incremental ML-KEM-768 layer and proposes to
**re-derive all of them from the bottom up**, starting from the
fundamental FIPS 203 mathematics rather than from the byte-length
contracts that the current specs encode.

The implementation under test is unchanged:
[`src/incremental_mlkem768.rs`](../../src/incremental_mlkem768.rs)
(functions/constants listed in
[`doc/truong/incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt`](../truong/incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt)),
a thin wrapper over `libcrux_ml_kem::mlkem768::incremental`,
instantiating the **ML-KEM-768** parameter set of FIPS 203 (Tables 2–3).

### What "discard and rebuild" means concretely

The current spec tree under
[`Spqr/Specs/IncrementalMlkem768/`](../../Spqr/Specs/IncrementalMlkem768/)
proves **size-only** postconditions (e.g. `result.length = 960`) against
**size-only** external models in
[`Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean`](../../Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean) that
return `default` byte buffers. Those specs are *true but shallow*: they
say nothing about *which bytes* a function produces or *why*. We treat
them as **deprecated scaffolding** and replace them with specifications
whose postconditions are *value-level* statements derived from a
verified mathematical core.

| Discarded artefact | Why discarded | Replaced by |
|--------------------|---------------|-------------|
| `*_spec` size-only theorems (`generate_spec`, `encaps1/2_spec`, `decaps_spec`, `ek_matches_header_spec`) | assert only byte lengths | new `*_spec` derived from the math core (sizes become corollaries) |
| size-only external models (`from_seed`/`encapsulate1/2`/`decapsulate…`/`validate_pk_bytes` returning `default`) | carry no cryptographic content | *computing* models that run the verified math definitions |
| stand-alone numeral theorems (`fips203_*_size`) | duplicate Table 3 numerals in isolation | length lemmas of the math core, specialised to ML-KEM-768 |
| local size axioms (`Ciphertext1_len_id`, `Result_is_ok_Ok`) | bridge to opaque `default` behaviour | discharged by the math core (no longer axiomatic) |

The only things retained from the prior work are the **extraction
itself** (`Spqr/Code/Funs.lean`, produced by Aeneas) and the proof of
`flip_endianness_of_encapsulation_state` (a pure byte-permutation fact
with no FIPS 203 content), which the new specs reuse unchanged.

### How this document is organised

The plan is **bottom-up**: Part A builds the mathematical foundation
(the "fundamental principles" from which everything derives); Part B
builds the FIPS 203 algorithms as functions over that foundation;
Part C wires those functions into *computing* external models; Part D
states the new value-level specifications; Part E gives the systematic
plan for eliminating every axiom and hypothesis from the current
verification; Part F gives the strict dependency-ordered build roadmap
and the project file layout.

**Important: Phase 0** is prepended before Parts A–F. It captures the
**immediate, no-math-required** concrete-model additions to
`FunsExternal.lean` that eliminate the easy axioms and hypotheses
*right now*, providing a quick win before the long-term math foundation
is built. This phase is fully decoupled from the FIPS 203 work.

Status legend: ✅ proved/`sorry`-free · ⚠️ stated with a tracked
`sorry` · ❌ not yet started. Feasibility: 🟢 now · 🟡 bounded ·
🟠 large · 🔴 research-scale.

