# Part D — The New Specifications for Every Function and Constant (`Spqr/Specs/IncrementalMlkem768/`)

We now **write the spec files fresh**, with **one new specification for
every entry of
[`doc/truong/incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt`](../truong/incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt)**
— all 8 functions and all 4 constants (the test entry is handled as a
runtime check, §D12). Every theorem is a *value-level* statement over
the Part-B reference functions; the old byte-length claims survive only
as trivial corollaries (via A3 length lemmas).

For each Rust function `f`, the new `f_spec` asserts: *`f`'s output
equals the Part-B reference function applied to the (decomposed)
inputs*, from which sizes and cross-object relationships follow. The
twelve subsections below correspond one-to-one with the source-of-truth
list.

## D1–D4. The four size constants (`*_SIZE.lean`, rewritten)

The constants are no longer proved by isolated `decide` against opaque
`len` axioms; each is re-derived as a **specialisation of an A3 length
