## D13. `Chain.lean` (new) — the KEM round-trip composition

Not a list entry itself, but the theorem tying D5–D9 together and giving
D12 its formal meaning:

```
mlkem_round_trip (seed coins : Bytes) :
  let K  := (encaps1 (generate seed).hdr coins).ss
  let c  := (encaps1 …).ct1 ‖ (encaps2 (generate seed).ek (encaps1 …).es)
  decaps (generate seed).dk c = K     -- on the high-probability event
```

`mlkemDecaps ∘ mlkemEncaps = id` is only *conditional* (decryption noise
< ⌈q/4⌋). Promoting it to the *unconditional* `K′ = K` requires the A8
failure bound — the single research-scale obligation, isolated cleanly
at the top of the stack. Depends on D5–D9, A8.

